Project Objective
The goal of the project is to deploy a series of eco-friendly parking lots and green stormwater management infrastructures on sites identified as vulnerable to heat waves and torrential rains. Priority intervention sites were selected based on the methodology prescribed by the Government of Québec.
With this financial contribution, Montreal will transform eight public parking lots into eco-friendly parking areas and create green stormwater management infrastructures on six additional sites.
Planned Activities for Eco-Friendly Parking Lots
These include:
Removal of impermeable mineral surfaces and their replacement with permeable paving materials featuring a higher solar reflectance index;
Development of vegetated swales;
Tree and plant planting, along with the installation of furniture that supports local biodiversity;
Installation of fixed amenities for rest, leisure, and active transportation.
The City aims to achieve at least the first level of the Eco-Friendly Parking Lot Certification.
Planned Activities for Green Stormwater Management Infrastructure
These will be tailored to the specific context of each intervention site and include:
Drainage swales and curb extensions;
Bioretention areas and rain gardens;
Blue-green alleys;
Resilient parks.
Expected Outcomes
The project is expected to:
Create or improve approximately 12,720 m² of green infrastructure;
Protect between 8,739 and 13,410 vulnerable individuals through these developments.

Interventions are proposed that can contribute to the disposal of rainwater collected by the school complex and the related parking area for a total surface area of 6000 m2:
- 140 m2 of rain garden for the infiltration of rainwater collected from school buildings, created in the areas pertaining to school buildings;
- 90 m3 accumulation tanks for the reuse of water collected from the roofs;
- 400 m3 dry detention basin inserted in the neighboring park area, sized for the rain accumulated from roofs and car parks during meteoric events with a return time of 10 years lasting <12h;
- Creation of 12 0m2 of bioretention strips to filter and infiltrate the water collected from the school car park.

